{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the inhabitant of the land, the Canaanite, saw.</b> That is Sihon and Og, for they too were called Canaanites, as Rashi explained in the portion of Shelach and of Shofetim and in several places." "<b>Which is across the Jordan.</b> That is the land of Canaan — that is, the inhabitants of the land of Sihon and Og saw the mourning at the threshing floor of Atad in the land of Canaan, which they call <b>across the Jordan</b>, for just as those dwelling in the land of Canaan that Joshua apportioned call the side of Sihon and Og 'across the Jordan,' so too those dwelling in the land of Sihon and Og call the land of Canaan 'across the Jordan,' as it is written in the portion of Matot: ״כי לא ננחל אותם מעבר לירדן והלאה כי באה נחלתנו אלינו מעבר הירדן מזרחה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:24.084614499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}